<%- include('../partials/head', { pageTitle, metaDescription, canonicalPath }) %>
<%- include('../partials/header') %>
<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Font &amp; image licences</h1>
      <p class="lede mt-1">Every creative asset on this site, where it came from, and what we are allowed to do with it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="alert alert--info" style="max-width:1000px;">
        <h2>How this register works</h2>
        <p>
          The register is a data file committed with the code, and the automated test suite fails if an image or font
          exists in <code>/public</code> without an entry here. That means an unlicensed file cannot be added quietly.
        </p>
        <p class="small">
          <strong>Important note on photography.</strong> The images in this build were generated for AESTHETICNOVA for
          this project. They are <em>not</em> photographs of the physical products being sold. They are illustrative,
          and they are labelled as illustrative on the product pages. Before launch, the business should replace the
          product images with original photography of the actual items — a real customer must see the real piece.
          The launch-readiness report records this as <strong>NEEDS HUMAN REVIEW</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="eyebrow mt-3">Asset register</h2>
      <table class="admin-table" style="background:#fff;">
        <caption class="sr-only">Licensing record for every image and font used on the site</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Asset</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Description</th>
            <th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Licence</th><th scope="col">Rights / attribution</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% assets.forEach(function (a) { %>
            <tr>
              <td><code><%= a.path %></code><% if (a.notes) { %><br><span class="small muted"><%= a.notes %></span><% } %></td>
              <td><%= a.type %></td>
              <td><%= a.description %></td>
              <td><%= a.source %></td>
              <td><%= a.licence %></td>
              <td><%= a.rights %><br><span class="small muted">Attribution: <%= a.attribution %></span></td>
            </tr>
          <% }); %>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 class="eyebrow mt-3">Fonts in detail</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <strong>Space Grotesk</strong> by Florian Karsten and <strong>Inter</strong> by Rasmus Andersson are both
          licensed under the <strong>SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1</strong>, which permits commercial use,
          modification and web embedding. Both are self-hosted from this domain — no request is made to Google’s
          servers, so no visitor IP is disclosed to a third party for typography.
        </p>
        <p>
          The OFL requires the licence text to accompany the font files when they are redistributed, so the full
          licence is served from this domain alongside the fonts themselves:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/fonts/LICENSE-space-grotesk.txt">SIL Open Font License 1.1 — Space Grotesk</a></li>
          <li><a href="/fonts/LICENSE-inter.txt">SIL Open Font License 1.1 — Inter</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="small muted">
          Both files are plain text, are not minified, and carry the copyright line for each project. Neither font has
          been modified: the woff2 files are the upstream releases, subset only by weight, so no Reserved Font Name
          issue arises.
        </p>

        <h2>Icons and interface graphics</h2>
        <p>
          All interface icons are inline SVG drawn for this project. There are no icon-font dependencies and no icon
          sets licensed from third parties, so there is nothing to attribute and nothing to leak through a CDN.
        </p>

        <h2>What is deliberately absent</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No competitor product photographs.</li>
          <li>No celebrity or influencer images.</li>
          <li>No fashion campaign images.</li>
          <li>No third-party brand logos, and no implied association with any other brand.</li>
          <li>No stock photography of models presented as AESTHETICNOVA customers.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Rights holder contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you believe an asset on this site infringes your rights, contact
          <strong><%= biz.email || 'support' %></strong> with the URL and the basis of your claim and we will respond
          promptly, including removing the asset while we investigate if the claim looks credible.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
<%- include('../partials/consent-banner') %>
</body>
</html>
